# Test File Location Rules

## Overview

This document defines **MANDATORY** test file locations. Every source file MUST have a corresponding test file in the specified location.

## Location Rules

### Model Tests

**Rule**: Every model MUST have a test file in `src/models/__tests__/`

**Pattern**: `src/models/{ModelName}.js` → `src/models/__tests__/{ModelName}.test.js`

**Examples**:
- `src/models/User.js` → `src/models/__tests__/User.test.js`
- `src/models/Company.js` → `src/models/__tests__/Company.test.js`
- `src/models/CompanyRole.js` → `src/models/__tests__/CompanyRole.test.js`

**Required**: ✅ Yes, for ALL models

---

### Repository Tests

**Rule**: Every repository MUST have a test file in `src/repositories/__tests__/`

**Pattern**: `src/repositories/{repositoryName}Repository.js` → `src/repositories/__tests__/{repositoryName}Repository.test.js`

**Examples**:
- `src/repositories/userRepository.js` → `src/repositories/__tests__/userRepository.test.js`
- `src/repositories/companyRepository.js` → `src/repositories/__tests__/companyRepository.test.js`

**Required**: ✅ Yes, for ALL repositories

**Note**: BaseRepository is tested implicitly through repository tests

---

### Service Tests

**Rule**: Every service MUST have a test file in `src/services/__tests__/`

**Pattern**: `src/services/{serviceName}Service.js` → `src/services/__tests__/{serviceName}Service.test.js`

**Examples**:
- `src/services/userService.js` → `src/services/__tests__/userService.test.js`
- `src/services/companyService.js` → `src/services/__tests__/companyService.test.js`

**Required**: ✅ Yes, for ALL services

**Exception**: `keycloakService.js` may need special handling (mocking Keycloak)

---

### Middleware Tests

**Rule**: Every middleware MUST have a test file in `src/middleware/__tests__/`

**Pattern**: `src/middleware/{middlewareName}.js` → `src/middleware/__tests__/{middlewareName}.test.js`

**Examples**:
- `src/middleware/authMiddleware.js` → `src/middleware/__tests__/authMiddleware.test.js`
- `src/middleware/errorHandler.js` → `src/middleware/__tests__/errorHandler.test.js`
- `src/middleware/validationMiddleware.js` → `src/middleware/__tests__/validationMiddleware.test.js`

**Required**: ✅ Yes, for ALL middleware

---

### Controller Tests

**Rule**: Every controller MUST have a test file in `src/modules/{module}/__tests__/`

**Pattern**: `src/modules/{module}/{module}Controller.js` → `src/modules/{module}/__tests__/{module}Controller.test.js`

**Examples**:
- `src/modules/auth/authController.js` → `src/modules/auth/__tests__/authController.test.js`
- `src/modules/users/userController.js` → `src/modules/users/__tests__/userController.test.js`
- `src/modules/admin/adminController.js` → `src/modules/admin/__tests__/adminController.test.js`

**Required**: ✅ Yes, for ALL controllers

**Note**: Tests are in the module's `__tests__` folder, NOT in a common `__tests__` folder

---

### Integration Tests

**Rule**: Every module with API endpoints MUST have an integration test file in `src/modules/__tests__/`

**Pattern**: `src/modules/{module}/` → `src/modules/__tests__/{module}.integration.test.js`

**Examples**:
- `src/modules/auth/` → `src/modules/__tests__/auth.integration.test.js`
- `src/modules/users/` → `src/modules/__tests__/users.integration.test.js`
- `src/modules/admin/` → `src/modules/__tests__/admin.integration.test.js`

**Required**: ✅ Yes, for ALL modules with API endpoints

**Note**: Integration tests are in the common `src/modules/__tests__/` folder

---

### Utility Tests

**Rule**: Every utility file MUST have a test file in `src/utils/__tests__/`

**Pattern**: `src/utils/{utilityName}.js` → `src/utils/__tests__/{utilityName}.test.js`

**Examples**:
- `src/utils/validators.js` → `src/utils/__tests__/validators.test.js`
- `src/utils/errors.js` → `src/utils/__tests__/errors.test.js`
- `src/utils/responseHelpers.js` → `src/utils/__tests__/responseHelpers.test.js`

**Required**: ✅ Yes, for ALL utility files

---

## File Naming Conventions

### Test File Names

- **Unit Tests**: `{SourceFileName}.test.js`
- **Integration Tests**: `{module}.integration.test.js`
- **Use camelCase**: Match source file naming

**Examples**:
- ✅ `User.test.js`
- ✅ `userRepository.test.js`
- ✅ `authController.test.js`
- ✅ `auth.integration.test.js`
- ❌ `user.test.js` (should match `User.js`)
- ❌ `UserRepository.test.js` (should match `userRepository.js`)

